  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset \"Genome - Pirum gemmata\" has garnered a single citation since its release in 2017, indicating initial scholarly uptake. This dataset has facilitated knowledge dissemination, as evidenced by its reuse in one published article and a mention in the biomedical literature.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Released in 2017 and hosted on Figshare, the dataset titled \"Genome - Pirum gemmata\" represents an effort in computational biology to elucidate genetic information pertinent to the species Pirum gemmata. Developed by the Multicellgenome Lab, this open-access resource aims to support further research in genetics and evolutionary biology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">To date, the dataset has been cited once in the academic literature, reflecting a nascent but promising engagement with the scholarly community. The citation originated from a 2025 article published in eLife focusing on G-protein-coupled receptors, signifying the dataset's relevance to contemporary biological research themes.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In addition to its citation, the dataset has been reused in another context, showcasing its broader applicability in the life sciences. It underscores the importance of shared genetic data in facilitating advancements across various research fields, notably in biology and computational approaches.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Despite initial low visibility\u2014evidenced by the absence of online mentions and downloads\u2014the dataset\u2019s foundational role in subsequent studies illustrates its potential for future scholarly inquiry. As the dataset continues to intersect with emerging research, its impact may grow, fostering a deeper understanding of complex genetic landscapes in organisms. Researchers and institutions involved in related fields should consider this resource for its potential applications in ongoing studies.</p>",
